    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// نجمع كل الأخبار حسب user_id\nconst grouped = {};\n\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const data = item.json;\n  const uid = data.user_id;\n\n  if (!grouped[uid]) {\n    grouped[uid] = [];\n  }\n  grouped[uid].push(data);\n}\n\n// نفرز كل مجموعة حسب التاريخ (الأحدث أول) وناخذ أول 5\nconst result = [];\n\nfor (const uid in grouped) {\n  const sorted = grouped[uid].sort((a, b) => {\n    return new Date(b.isoDate) - new Date(a.isoDate);\n  });\n\n  const latest5 = sorted.slice(0, 1);\n\n  for (const news of latest5) {\n    result.push({ json: news });\n  }\n}\n\nreturn result;"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        896,
        -96
      ],
      "id": "3151dcd4-2371-4467-a247-6e2eae6d460d",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze this news item for the user:\n\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nContent: {{ $json.content }}\nAdditional context: {{ $json.extra_description }}\nLink: {{ $json.link }}\nPublished: {{ $json.pubDate }}\n\nUser interests: {{ $json.interests }}\nUser ID: {{ $json.user_id }}\nMinimum score required: {{ $json.min_score }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a content opportunity assistant. Your job is to analyze one \nnews item and decide whether it matches a specific user's interests \nclosely enough to become a content opportunity.\n\nInput data you receive for each news item:\n- title, content, link, pubDate: details of the news item\n- interests: the user's stated interests (comma-separated)\n- user_id: unique identifier for the user\n- min_score: the minimum opportunity score this user accepts (0-100)\n\nSteps to follow:\n1. Evaluate how relevant the news item is to the user's interests and \n   assign an Opportunity Score from 0 to 100.\n2. If the score is below min_score, return \"should_send\": false with a \n   short reason.\n3. If the score meets or exceeds min_score, write:\n   - a short reason (2-3 sentences) explaining why this news matters to \n     this specific user\n   - a suggested post ready for publishing, written in Arabic. Keep it \n  concise (under 280 characters) so it works well across platforms \n  like X and LinkedIn - the user can adapt the tone if needed.\n4. Only if you decide should_send is true, use the Google Sheets tool \n   to append a new row with user_id, news_link (the article link), and \n   today's date to the Sent News Log sheet.\n\nStrict rules:\n- Never invent information not present in the original news content.\n- If the news data is incomplete (missing title or content), return \n  \"error\": \"incomplete news data\" and do not attempt analysis.\n- Always return the result as JSON only, with no extra text outside \n  the JSON object.\n-Call the Google Sheets tool exactly once, only after your final \ndecision on should_send. Never call it more than once per news item.\n\nRequired output format (JSON only):\n{\n  \"should_send\": true,\n  \"score\": 85,\n  \"reason\": \"short explanation of why this news matters to this user\",\n  \"suggested_content\": \"the suggested post text in Arabic\"\n}"
        }
      },
